================================================================
 platform-enable-msm — wire up drivers/platform/msm/ subdirectory
================================================================

 Two-line additions to vanilla mainline 6.19:
   drivers/platform/Kconfig  — add 'source "drivers/platform/msm/Kconfig"'
   drivers/platform/Makefile — add 'obj-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM) += msm/'

 Without these, the kernel build system never descends into the
 drivers/platform/msm/ subdirectory we ship in vendor-baseline-4.19/
 — and our IPA driver, BAM/SPS framework, and Kconfig options all
 stay invisible.

 The drivers/platform/msm/Kconfig and drivers/platform/msm/Makefile
 themselves are NEW (minimal 4-line and 2-line versions sourcing
 only sps/ and ipa/) and ship in vendor-baseline-4.19/.

 Standalone patch, applies to vanilla mainline 6.19.

================================================================

--- a/drivers/platform/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/platform/Kconfig
@@ -23,3 +23,4 @@
 
 source "drivers/platform/wmi/Kconfig"
 
+source "drivers/platform/msm/Kconfig"
--- a/drivers/platform/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/platform/Makefile
@@ -15,3 +15,4 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_ARM64_PLATFORM_DEVICES)	+= arm64/
 obj-$(CONFIG_BCM2835_VCHIQ)	+= raspberrypi/
 obj-$(CONFIG_ACPI_WMI)		+= wmi/
+obj-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM) += msm/
